  "findings": [
    "Measured baseline medians: staging 2052 ms, production 2141 ms. The 89 ms difference does not establish a meaningful environment regression in these small sequential cohorts.",
    "All 15 measured production registrations completed within 2500 ms. This is a sample result, not a latency guarantee.",
    "The first production warm-up registration took 6769 ms. Respond took 5021 ms and finalize 1313 ms.",
    "That request included Deriver A protocol elapsed 2885 ms within an invocation reporting 245 ms CPU and 3214 ms wall time. Deriver B reported 2784 ms protocol,216 ms CPU,2967 ms wall.",
    "These spans contain waits. The first-request delay is not explained by reported invocation CPU alone; the traces do not identify network, storage, output gating, scheduling, or cold-start causality."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Sequential cohorts cannot fully control temporal variation. Staging and production use different tenants and testnet/mainnet configuration.",
    "Three warm-up samples are recorded separately; omitting them from the baseline does not remove their user-visible latency.",
    "The third production warm-up Deriver B protocol trace is absent. Complete trace coverage is not established.",
    "The historical 0.13 benchmark served both parent and iframe locally. Its 66 samples excluded 3 warm-ups. It is not a matched SDK or environment comparison with this hosted-iframe measurement."
  ],
